{
  "title": "Courier Round Trip Budget",
  "description": "## Task\n\nA courier starts at depot 0, must visit every other stop exactly once, and then returns to depot 0. `dist[i][j]` is the cost of driving from stop `i` to stop `j` (it need not equal `dist[j][i]`). Find the cheapest complete round trip. Checking every visiting order is far too slow for the larger inputs.\n\n## Input\n\n- `dist` — a square matrix of non-negative integers; `dist[i][i]` is 0. Stop 0 is the depot.\n\n## Output\n\nThe minimum total cost of a tour that leaves 0, visits all stops once and returns to 0. With a single stop the answer is 0.\n\n## Example\n\n```python\ncourier_round_trip([[0, 1], [2, 0]])  # returns 3\ncourier_round_trip([[0]])  # returns 0\ncourier_round_trip([[0, 5, 9], [5, 0, 1], [9, 1, 0]])  # returns 15\n```\n\n## Constraints\n\n- 1 ≤ number of stops ≤ 16\n- 0 ≤ each cost ≤ 10^6\n",
  "signature": "def courier_round_trip(dist: list[list[int]]) -> int",
  "topic": "bitmask dp",
  "difficulty": "hard",
